course: dictionary
lesson: 5095
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Interest is one of them. To find the right meaning, read the words around it and ask which meaning fits the sentence.
explain: «Bertie mutters, "It's giving zero interest."» Here "it's giving" means it looks like, so Bertie thinks the thing looks dull. Interest means the feeling of wanting to know more, and it is missing.
explain: «If a strange dog runs at you, stand still and stay quiet until it loses interest.» The dog stops wanting to chase you. Interest here means its attention, the feeling that keeps it going. When the feeling goes, the dog leaves you alone.
explain: «If a bank pays 10% interest on $100, you get $10 extra.» This is the money meaning. The bank adds extra money to your savings, and that extra money is called interest.
fact: Interest can mean the feeling of wanting to know more about something.
fact: An interest is something you like doing or learning about, like a hobby.
fact: In money, interest is extra money a bank pays you for saving, or extra money you pay when you borrow.
fact: To interest someone means to make them want to know more.
fact: Useful phrases: take an interest in, show interest, lose interest, and interest rate.
exercise: «Gaming guides, magazines and fact books are real reading too; interest is what keeps a reader going.» What does interest mean here? | A rule about reading | A sad, grey mood | Extra money paid by a bank | *The feeling of wanting to read on
exercise: «If a bank pays 10% interest on $100, you get $10 extra.» How much extra money do you get? | $100 | $20 | $1 | *$10
exercise: In «Tom's main interest is dinosaurs», what does interest mean? | Money he has saved in the bank | A dinosaur book he has lost | A feeling of being tired | *Something he likes doing or learning about
test:
«It's giving zero interest,» Bertie mutters. What does Bertie mean? | *It looks dull and boring | It looks very bright and shiny | It is giving away free money | It costs a lot of money
«If a strange dog runs at you, stay quiet until it loses interest.» What does loses interest mean? | It writes a letter to you | It starts to bark much louder | *It stops paying attention to you | It runs away with your bag
exam:
In «teasing about interests makes people hide what they enjoy», what does interests mean? | Extra money paid by a bank | *Things people like doing or learning about | Feelings of sleepiness | Rules that people must follow
